# Local development defaults (Vite). Copy to .env (gitignored).
#
# Prefer calling Spring Boot directly during local UI work:
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Optional same-origin style locally: set VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api and use the Vite
# proxy (see vite.config.ts), which strips /api before forwarding to the API.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# Google Sign-In — must match the backend GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID (same OAuth 2.0 Web client ID).
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create OAuth client ID → Web application.
# Authorized JavaScript origins: http://localhost:5173 (and http://127.0.0.1:5173 if you use it)
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Optional: Vite dev server proxy target (see vite.config.ts)
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8080

# Production note: the frontend Docker image builds with VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
# (see mentor-marketplace-web/Dockerfile and root docker-compose.yml). Do not bake
# secrets into the SPA image; Google client ID is public browser config only.
